{
	"Name": "Flow - Okta - Alert Router - Email Notification",
	"Description": "The single consumer on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Emails every Okta detection\nthat fires to one place.\n\nThree nodes:\n  1. MacroGet reads $GRAVWELL_INSTANCE, $OKTA_ALERT_SENDER, and\n     $OKTA_ALERT_RECIPIENT.\n  2. Template renders an HTML summary. The subject and heading come from the\n     dispatching scheduled search's name, so the detection names itself. The body\n     lists every field on the event, which for the raw-entry detections is the\n     whole Okta System Log extraction.\n  3. Email sends it.\n\nBefore enabling:\n  - Set the three configuration macros above.\n  - Configure Account \u003e Email Server \u003e Email Server Settings.\n\nTo notify somewhere other than email, add a Slack, Teams, Mattermost, Google Chat,\nor PagerDuty node to this flow. Because every detection routes through the one\nalert, wiring it once here covers all of them.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://docs.gravwell.io/flows/flows.html\n- https://docs.gravwell.io/alerts/alerts.html",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "flow",
	"GUID": "0ac35f09-fa74-49ee-977a-3b2fcb1b3b50",
